.TH SKIFFLLM 1 "2026-09-04" "SkiffLLM 1.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skiffllm \- offline-first local LLM terminal assistant built on llama.cpp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skiffllm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fImodel.gguf\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SkiffLLM runs a local GGUF language model entirely on your machine. It supports
interactive chat, one-shot prompts, named sessions, JSON output, sampling
profiles, stop sequences, and automatic context management.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-model <path>\fR
Path to a GGUF model file.
.TP
\fB\-\-model-dir <path>\fR
Directory scanned for a GGUF model.
.TP
\fB\-\-list-models\fR
Print discovered GGUF models.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile <name>\fR
Use balanced, fast, creative, code, or precise sampling profile.
.TP
\fB\-\-session <name>\fR
Use a named conversation.
.TP
\fB\-\-system <text> (alias: \-\-system-prompt)\fR
Set the system prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-project <dir>\fR
Add a bounded project context block before a one-shot prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-history <path>\fR
Session/history file (default under ~/.local/share/skiffllm).
.TP
\fB\-\-save / \-\-no-save\fR
Enable or disable persisting the conversation. Saving is enabled by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto-trim / \-\-no-auto-trim\fR
Trim old history when the context is full. Auto-trim is enabled by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-stop <text>\fR
Add a stop sequence. May be repeated.
.TP
\fB\-\-attach <path>\fR
Attach a file to the prompt. May be repeated.
.TP
\fB\-\-file <path>\fR
Alias for --attach.
.TP
\fB\-\-chat-template <name>\fR
Override the model chat template.
.TP
\fB\-\-export <path>\fR
Export the loaded conversation as Markdown.
.TP
\fB\-\-warmup\fR
Warm the model before the first answer.
.TP
\fB\-\-summarize <file>\fR
Summarize a file as a one-shot document task.
.TP
\fB\-\-remember <text>\fR
Save a persistent memory line for future sessions.
.TP
\fB\-\-forget <text>\fR
Remove matching persistent memory lines.
.TP
\fB\-\-code\fR
Propose concrete unified-diff edits without modifying files.
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
With --doctor, print network/privacy facts.
.TP
\fB\-\-serve\fR
Serve a local OpenAI-compatible HTTP API.
.TP
\fB\-\-host <addr>\fR
Local server bind address. Default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
\fB\-\-port <n>\fR
Local server port. Default is 8080.
.TP
\fB\-\-api-key <key>\fR
Require Authorization: Bearer <key> on /v1/models and
/v1/chat/completions. /health, /version, and / stay public.
.TP
\fB\-\-benchmark <runs>\fR
Run a real generation benchmark with the given number of runs.
.TP
\fB\-\-ctx <n>\fR
Context size. Default is 4096.
.TP
\fB\-\-batch <n>\fR
Batch size. Default is 512.
.TP
\fB\-\-ubatch <n>\fR
Physical batch size.
.TP
\fB\-\-threads <n>\fR
CPU threads. Zero means auto.
.TP
\fB\-\-gpu-layers <n>\fR
GPU layers to offload. Negative means all.
.TP
\fB\-\-mmap / \-\-no-mmap\fR
Enable or disable mmap.
.TP
\fB\-\-mlock\fR
Lock model memory into RAM.
.TP
\fB\-\-flash-attn / \-\-no-flash-attn\fR
Enable or disable flash attention.
.TP
\fB\-\-numa\fR
Initialize NUMA optimization.
.TP
\fB\-\-kv-offload / \-\-no-kv-offload\fR
Control KV cache offloading.
.TP
\fB\-\-temp <t> (alias: \-\-temperature)\fR
Sampling temperature.
.TP
\fB\-\-top-p <p>\fR
Nucleus sampling probability.
.TP
\fB\-\-top-k <n>\fR
Top-k sampling value.
.TP
\fB\-\-min-p <p>\fR
Minimum probability filter.
.TP
\fB\-\-typical <p>\fR
Locally typical sampling value.
.TP
\fB\-\-repeat-penalty <p>\fR
Repeat penalty.
.TP
\fB\-\-repeat-last-n <n>\fR
Repeat penalty window.
.TP
\fB\-\-n-predict <n> (alias: \-\-n)\fR
Maximum generated tokens.
.TP
\fB\-\-seed <n|random>\fR
Sampling seed.
.TP
\fB\-\-prompt <text>\fR
Run a single prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-prompt-file <path>\fR
Read the prompt from a file.
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
Read the prompt from stdin.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine-readable JSON output.
.TP
\fB\-\-output <path>\fR
Write the answer to a file.
.TP
\fB\-\-model-info\fR
Print model metadata and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-smoke\fR
Run a quick generation smoke test.
.TP
\fB\-\-tokenize <text>\fR
Tokenize text and print token counts.
.TP
\fB\-\-doctor\fR
Print system diagnostics.
.TP
\fB\-\-config <path>\fR
Use the given config file.
.TP
\fB\-\-show-config\fR
Print the effective configuration. With \fB\-\-json\fR, emit JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-context-bar / \-\-no-context-bar\fR
Enable or disable the live context usage bar. Enabled by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-backend-info\fR
Print the llama.cpp backends linked into this build and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show help.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show version.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B skiffllm run [prompt] [options]
Run a one-shot prompt, e.g. skiffllm run "Merhaba" --ctx 2048 --temp 0.3.
.TP
.B skiffllm model list|info|install|remove|verify
Manage the local model catalog and verify downloaded GGUF files.
.TP
.B skiffllm chat-template list|detect|info
List known chat templates or detect the template embedded in a model.
.TP
.B skiffllm openai [prompt] [options]
Send a prompt to a local OpenAI-compatible server, e.g. skiffllm openai "Hi" --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080. This is an explicit network client; it transmits the prompt to the server you choose.
.TP
.B skiffllm config path|show|init
Print, inspect, or write the configuration file.
.TP
.B skiffllm server health [--json]
Check a running local server.
.TP
.B skiffllm session list|show|rename|remove
Manage named conversations.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_MODEL\fR
Default model path.
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_MODEL_DIR\fR
Default model directory.
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_CONFIG\fR
Config file path.
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_HISTORY\fR
History file path.
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_SYSTEM\fR
Default system prompt.
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_PROFILE\fR
Default sampling profile.
.TP
\fBSKIFFLLM_API_KEY\fR
Bearer token for --serve.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/skiffllm/config\fR
Default configuration file.
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/skiffllm/models/\fR
Default model directory.
.TP
\fB~/.local/share/skiffllm/history.skif\fR
Default session history.
.SH SERVER
.TP
The server binds to localhost by default and exposes /health, /v1/models, and
/v1/chat/completions. Fast endpoints answer while generation is serialized.
With --api-key, /v1/* requires Authorization: Bearer <key>; /health,
/version, and / stay public.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B /help, /info, /history
Show help, session details, or the current conversation.
.TP
.B /remember <fact>, /forget <text>
Persist or remove a user memory. /memories lists; /clear-memories clears.
.TP
.B /file <path>, /clear-attach
Attach a file or clear attached files.
.TP
.B /export <path>
Export the conversation as Markdown.
.TP
.B /tokenize <text>
Show the token count for the text.
.TP
.B /settings, /profile, /stop
Show or change sampling settings.
.TP
.B /temp, /top-p, /top-k, /min-p, /typical, /n, /ctx
Change sampling and context values.
.TP
.B /save, /clear, /reset, /system, /model
Manage the session and model.
.TP
.B /exit or /quit
Exit SkiffLLM.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. Non-zero on configuration or inference errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama.cpp
local inference documentation, and the project README for full usage.
